Maintainer: Chia-Jung Chang <charlene.cj.chang@gmail.com>
Description: Annotates the cells of a tumour sample along a four-level cell-type
    hierarchy, scored against a pan-cancer marker database in which every core
    marker is supported by at least three independent public sources (database
    v3.3; v3.2 is included to reproduce the initial version). Markers are not
    asked to decide malignancy: the epithelial lineage is split into malignant
    and normal epithelium by a copy-number signal inferred within the sample
    against the sample's own immune cells, after a sample-level test of whether
    a tumour is present at all; when the test is negative no cell is called
    malignant. 'sconco()' runs one sample, 'sconco_study()' every sample of a
    study with a cross-sample immune reference for samples with too few immune
    cells of their own, and 'sconco_seurat()' works on a 'Seurat' object. The
    functions of the earlier flat marker-scoring framework ('run_scONCO()' and
    its confidence layer) are kept to reproduce the benchmark.
